# Copy this file to .env in this same folder (vectors/prompt_injection/.env)
# and fill in real values. .env is gitignored - never commit real keys.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Nothing here is required to run this vector at all: with no .env present,
# both the target agent and the attacker default to a local qwen3:8b model
# via Ollama (see README.md's Setup section for the `ollama pull` step).
# Everything below is only for testing the ATTACKER on the Gemini API
# instead - see README.md's "Using the Gemini API" section for the full
# picture, including why the target agent can't be switched this way.

# --- Gemini API keys (optional) ---
# Only needed if you want to run the attacker on a real API model instead of
# local Qwen3-8B. Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey.
GEMINI_API_KEY=your-gemini-api-key-here

# Optional extra keys - if the first key hits its daily quota (a 429), the
# client fails over to the next one instead of retrying a dead key. Add as
# many as you have; _2, _3, _4, ... are picked up automatically until one is
# unset. More keys = more daily quota, not faster calls (see
# ADL_GEMINI_MIN_INTERVAL below, which is shared across all of them).
# GEMINI_API_KEY_2=your-second-gemini-api-key-here
# GEMINI_API_KEY_3=your-third-gemini-api-key-here

# --- Which model each role uses ---
# Uncomment to switch the ATTACKER (red team / MAP-Elites mutation operator)
# from local Qwen3-8B to Gemini. Requires GEMINI_API_KEY above to be set.
# The target agent always stays on the local model regardless of this
# setting - it isn't wired to read this variable at all (see agent.py).
# ADL_ATTACKER_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# Override the local Ollama model for both the target agent and (when
# ADL_ATTACKER_MODEL is unset) the attacker. Defaults to qwen3:8b.
# ADL_LOCAL_MODEL=qwen3:8b

# --- Gemini call pacing ---
# Minimum seconds between Gemini calls, shared across every configured key.
# Free-tier gemini-2.5-flash is capped at 10 requests/minute per key; the
# default of 6.5s keeps a run under that limit on its own. Only change this
# if you're on a paid tier with a higher rate limit.
# ADL_GEMINI_MIN_INTERVAL=6.5
